  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Plotting the given value in diagram we have,</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0079_0fececfad620.png\" style=\"width: 383px; height: 338px;\" /></p><p>Now let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;be a point on&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>, so area formed by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#9651;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;will be,</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#916;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mi>x</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>y</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>And area of triangle formed by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#9651;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;will be,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#916;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>36</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>&#916;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>&#916;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mn>36</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>14</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>35</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>95</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8943;</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Equation of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;by two point form will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8943;</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Solving&nbsp;equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;we get,</p><p>Point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow><mn>7</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now equation of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>11</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>20</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>,</p><p>So <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo></math>intercept will be&nbsp;point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and similarly from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;we get&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>So Area of triangle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}